stateDiagram-v2
  direction LR
  [*] --> NEW: spawn()
  NEW --> READY: admitted, assigned a CPU

  READY --> RUNNING: dispatched (front of its core's highest queue)
  RUNNING --> READY: quantum expired (demote one level)
  RUNNING --> READY: preempted by a higher queue on the same core

  RUNNING --> WAITING: CPU burst ended, I/O submitted
  RUNNING --> WAITING: pipe full (writer) or empty (reader)
  WAITING --> READY: wake() — same queue level, no demotion

  RUNNING --> TERMINATED: last burst finished
  READY --> TERMINATED: kill()
  WAITING --> TERMINATED: kill()

  READY --> STOPPED: SIGSTOP
  RUNNING --> STOPPED: SIGSTOP
  WAITING --> STOPPED: SIGSTOP (stays blocked)
  STOPPED --> READY: SIGCONT
  STOPPED --> WAITING: SIGCONT, if it was blocked
  TERMINATED --> [*]
